  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Praveen Kumar (Prop. Deepak Sweets) vs The State Of Jharkhand on 8 December, 2025 Author: Anil Kumar Choudhary Bench: Anil Kumar Choudhary (2025:Jhhc:3 In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr.M.P. No.4107 of 2023 ------ Praveen Kumar (Prop. Deepak Sweets), aged about 53 years, Son of Shiv Prasad Sah, Resident of Near Old Bus Stand, Chandandih, Latehar, P.O. & P.S.- Latehar, District- Latehar, Jharkhand (829206) ... Petitioner Versus 1. The State of Jharkhand 2. Food Safety Officer, Latehar ... Opposite Parties ------ For the Petitioner : Mr. Ashutosh Ranjan Kumar, Advocate For the State : Mr. Prabhu D. Agrawal, Spl. P.P. ------ Present Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Anil Kumar Choudhary By the Court:- Heard the parties. 2.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the relevant penal clause is Section 59 (i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Section 3 (1) (ZZ) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is a definition clause, which defines 'unsafe food', so, when a sense having (2025:JHHC:36773) been taken in respect of a provision of law which is not a penal provision, the Praveen Kumar (Prop. Deepak Sweets) vs The State Of Jharkhand on 8 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/21294478/ 1 impugned order is not sustainable in law. 4. Learned Spl. P.P. appearing for the State fairly submits that Section 3 (1) (ZZ) (viii) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is not a penal provision of law.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the relevant penal clause is Section 59 (i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Section 3 (1) (ZZ) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is a definition clause, which defines 'unsafe food', so, when a sense having (2025:JHHC:36773) been taken in respect of a provision of law which is not a penal provision, the Praveen Kumar (Prop. Deepak Sweets) vs The State Of Jharkhand on 8 December, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/21294478/ 1 impugned order is not sustainable in law. 4. Learned Spl. P.P. appearing for the State fairly submits that Section 3 (1) (ZZ) (viii) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is not a penal provision of law.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
